            "claim_id": "c1",
            "status": "introduced",
            "necessary": "yes",
            "before": {
              "requirement": "Initialize notes before the assembly pass allocates section information.",
              "applicability": "required",
              "harness_status": "sat",
              "reason": "The old harness calls read_begin, which initialized notes before the pass.",
              "source_evidence": [
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-e1b0b6fc88128e80a39a265a",
                  "quote": "  /* Something close -- but not too close -- to a multiple of 1024.\n     The debugging malloc I'm using has 24 bytes of overhead.  */\n  obstack_begin (&notes, chunksize);\n  obstack_begin (&cond_obstack, chunksize);\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-bf9313443683a32d2878e0d8",
                  "quote": "static void\nalloc_seginfo (segT seg)\n{\n  segment_info_type *seginfo;\n\n  seginfo = obstack_alloc (&notes, sizeof (*seginfo));\n  memset (seginfo, 0, sizeof (*seginfo));\n  seginfo->bfd_section = seg;\n  bfd_set_section_userdata (seg, seginfo);\n}\n"
                }
              ]
            },
            "after": {
              "requirement": "Initialize notes before the assembly pass allocates section information, now through the initialization in main or an equivalent call.",
              "applicability": "required",
              "harness_status": "unsat",
              "reason": "read_begin no longer initializes notes. The unchanged harness bypasses main, where initialization now occurs, and reaches section allocation without it.",
              "source_evidence": [
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-429ad8ed0938cdc556d18bf4",
                  "quote": "void\nread_begin (void)\n{\n  const char *p;\n\n  pobegin ();\n  obj_read_begin_hook ();\n\n  obstack_begin (&cond_obstack, chunksize);\n\n#ifndef tc_line_separator_chars\n#define tc_line_separator_chars line_separator_chars\n#endif\n  /* Use machine dependent syntax.  */\n  for (p = tc_line_separator_chars; *p; p++)\n    is_end_of_line[(unsigned char) *p] = 2;\n  /* Use more.  FIXME-SOMEDAY.  */\n\n  if (flag_mri)\n    lex_type['?'] = 3;\n}\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-eae0e11cdccd2e8c87c743e8",
                  "quote": "  obstack_begin (&notes, chunksize);\n  xatexit (free_notes);\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-310a77f69eba4319a3f06d45",
                  "quote": "static void\nalloc_seginfo (segT seg)\n{\n  segment_info_type *seginfo;\n\n  seginfo = obstack_alloc (&notes, sizeof (*seginfo));\n  memset (seginfo, 0, sizeof (*seginfo));\n  seginfo->bfd_section = seg;\n  bfd_set_section_userdata (seg, seginfo);\n}\n"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_id": "loc-26883eeb5fa6e1f99907b6ed",
                  "quote": "#ifndef OBJ_MACH_O\n  /* Create the standard sections, and those the assembler uses\n     internally.  */\n  text_section = subseg_new (TEXT_SECTION_NAME, 0);\n  data_section = subseg_new (DATA_SECTION_NAME, 0);\n  bss_section = subseg_new (BSS_SECTION_NAME, 0);\n"
                }
              ]
            },
            "same_blocker": "not_applicable",
            "reason": "The before-side initialization was reachable through read_begin; the after-side initialization is in main, which the fixed old harness does not call.",
